  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "Amber Town sits on the eastern shore of Lake Yantar, a broad and shallow body of water whose amber-colored shallows give the settlement its name.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The town is a knot of wooden houses, market stalls, and warehouses clustered around a central pier where barges tie up to unload their cargo.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Amber Town is the largest trading hub between the river Vesna and the northern pine forests, serving as a waypoint where goods from the deep north meet the southbound barges.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "history",
      "text": "Founded shortly after the Night of Feathers in 994, when the town's first buildings were raised by owl-folk settlers who came south to trade.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "law",
      "text": "The town falls under the jurisdiction of the Tsardom of Moscavia and pays an annual tithe in amber and furs to the Tsar's treasury in Kremova.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The market square, called the Ploshchad Solntsa, is paved with flat river stones and dominated by the tall amber-lantern post at its center, which burns every evening to guide barges into the pier.",
      "since": 1005
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Most of the town's inhabitants are owl-folk, though a handful of human traders from the southern ports maintain permanent residences here.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The town's wealth comes primarily from the amber trade — raw pieces pulled from the lake's shallows and polished pieces carved by local artisans — but it also handles timber, pelts, dried fish, and honey.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "There is a single inn, the Sova's Rest, run by an owl-folk widow named Marfa, whose rooftop gallery overlooks the lake and serves as a popular evening gathering spot.",
      "since": 1002
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The lake itself is rich with amber-bearing strata beneath its silty bottom; on calm days, pieces can be seen glinting just below the surface, and children often wade in to collect them.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Amber Town has no walls or fortifications, relying instead on its position at the head of navigation on the Vesna and its good relations with neighboring communities.",
      "since": 994
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Each autumn, the town hosts the Yantarnaya Yarmarka, a three-day trading fair that draws merchants and travelers from across Moscavia and beyond.",
      "since": 1008
    }
  ],
